Fixed the two protocol findings in d7772150bcd: supported v4 nodes retain their approved plugin capabilities, commands, and surface URLs; Linux and Rust clients consume the canonical v5/v4 constants. Rust also preserves the selected v4 session protocol when the accepted hello reports a v5 server. The real-Gateway regression now exercises v4 plugin URL access and invocation.

Local proof: 21 node-policy tests, 10 Rust node-session tests, one lifecycle test, and the signing/device-token recovery tests pass. Final independent review is clean at P0–P2. The replacement head's full CI remains pending; prior-head failures and matching baseline evidence remain documented separately.

@clawsweeper re-review

The registered-row preservation finding is fixed: Doctor backs up non-A2UI registered rows and converts them to inert escaped HTML previews, retaining original source/metadata while clearing capabilities. The production-store regression covers registered-only databases as well as both A2UI deletion markers.

The latest head also fixes the context-meter test's animation/crop measurement race without changing its painted-color assertions. Both repairs passed focused proof and independent review. The PR body records the details and the current full CI run.

